  "title": "Erdős Problem #711",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $f(n,m)$ be minimal such that in $(m,m+f(n,m))$ there exist distinct integers $a_1,\\ldots,a_n$ such that $k\\mid a_k$ for all $1\\leq k\\leq n$. Prove that $ \\max_m f(n,m) \\leq n^{1+o(1)} $ and that $ \\max_m (f(n,m)-f(n,n))\\to \\infty. $ ",
